From 8e7e770faccdff74dfcd76e1a50083e92f64c401 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel-experiments <kernel-experiments@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:25:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] cuda: grouped-query q8_0 decode attention with per-head
 masks (opt-in GGML_CUDA_INK_T_FAGQA)

llama.cpp packs GQA heads only when all heads share one mask; Inkling 2 has a per-head relative-position bias
(mask ne[2] = 24), so every query head re-loaded and re-dequantized its KV head (ncu 8K: 66 MB L2 reads for a
20.7 MB KV, 244 regs, 24% occupancy). fattn-vec-gqa.cu is generated from fattn-vec.cuh (asserted replacements):
the 3 query heads of a KV head are the kernel columns, each with its own mask row and sink.
- mode 1: stock KV split -> same bits, but 3x fewer blocks: slower (0K 61.43 vs 63.02/62.73).
- mode 2: KV split retuned to one block per KV head, used for n_kv >= 4096: 8K 57.37 vs 56.84/56.62,
  32K 52.08 vs 49.42/49.35 (+5.4%). Not bit-exact (combine order): Inkling-shape FA tests pass at NMSE 1e-6
  for both stock and mode 2; ~7K-token greedy decode identical tokens, logprob delta <= 0.16.
Default off (bit-exact build). Adds test_flash_attn_ext_ink (INK_FA_NMSE tolerance override).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn-vec-gqa.cu         | 648 ++++++++++++++++++++
